# ===========================================================================
# .env.example — TEMPLATE ONLY. NEVER COMMIT REAL VALUES.
#
# README §2 rule 7: "No secrets in the repo. Never commit API keys, tokens,
# credentials, or .env files. Use .env.example and .gitignore."
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env      # then fill in real values locally
#
# .env is gitignored. Every value in THIS file must be a placeholder or an
# empty string. If you find a real credential in here, that is a leak —
# rotate it and tell the human operator.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS: no code in this repository consumes any of these variables yet.
#
# This file exists to establish the convention before the first agent that
# needs a credential lands. Variable names are added ALONGSIDE the code that
# reads them, in the same PR — not speculatively. Inventing variable names
# for services that do not exist yet would be guessing, which README §2
# rule 2 forbids.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Scraping / data sources (tools/scrapers/) -----------------------------
# README §6 lists Takealot and Google Trends ZA as scraper targets.
# No keys required yet. Add here only when a scraper genuinely needs one,
# with a justification in the PR that introduces it (README §10).

# --- Payments (PayFast / SnapScan) -----------------------------------------
# Mentioned in README §4 as relevant SA rails. Not consumed by any code yet.

# --- Ad platforms ----------------------------------------------------------
# Not consumed by any code yet. Any ad spend requires a HITL gate (README §5)
# before it happens, regardless of what credentials exist.
